.TH LALBURST_INJ_PIC "1" "January 2026" "LALBurst" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lalburst_inj_pic \- Convert an image into a LIGO Light-Weight XML file containing a list of sine-
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lalburst_inj_pic.py
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,filename\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert an image into a LIGO Light\-Weight XML file containing a list of sineGaussian burst injections.  When injected into data, the injections will cause
a waterfall plot to display the image.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-l\fR Hz, \fB\-\-f\-low\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Set the low\-frequency limit of the tiling in Hertz
(default = 64).
.TP
\fB\-d\fR Hz, \fB\-\-delta\-f\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Set the bandwidth of the pixels in Hertz (default =
16).  Must be > 0.  The product of \fB\-\-delta\-f\fR and
\fB\-\-delta\-t\fR must be at least 2/pi.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR s, \fB\-\-delta\-t\fR=\fI\,s\/\fR
Set the duration of the pixels in seconds (default =
1/16).  Must be > 0.  The product of \fB\-\-delta\-f\fR and
\fB\-\-delta\-t\fR must be at least 2/pi.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR fraction, \fB\-\-overlap\-fraction\fR=\fI\,fraction\/\fR
Set the fraction by which adjacent tiles overlap
(default = 0.25).  The pixels centres are spaced (1 \-
\fB\-\-overlap\-fraction\fR) * \fB\-\-delta\-f\fR apart in the frequency
domain.  The value must be in the range [0, 1).
.TP
\fB\-H\fR pixels, \fB\-\-height\fR=\fI\,pixels\/\fR
Set the number of pixles in the frequency domain
(default = 64).  The image will be scaled to this
vertical size, and the number of pixels in the time
domain (horizontal size) will be fixed by the image
aspect ratio.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR filename, \fB\-\-output\fR=\fI\,filename\/\fR
Set the name of the output file (default = stdout).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR seconds, \fB\-\-gps\-start\-time\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Set the start time of the tiling in GPS seconds
(required).
.TP
\fB\-\-sample\-rate\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Set the sample rate in Hertz of the data into which
the injections will be placed (default = 16384).  This
information is required in order to normalize each
pixel accurately.  If the wrong value is used, the
result will be the addition of noise to the image.
The highest frequency pixel must have a centre
frequency < 1/2 this frequency.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR hrss, \fB\-\-hrss\-scale\fR=\fI\,hrss\/\fR
Set the single\-pixel hrss (root\-sum\-square strain)
corresponding to "white" (default = 1e\-20).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Be verbose.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR filename, \fB\-\-time\-slide\-xml\fR=\fI\,filename\/\fR
Associate injections with the first time slide ID in
this XML file (required).
